{"step_index":192,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T11:57:45Z","input_tokens":3031,"cache_read_tokens":118798,"output_tokens":692,"content":"**No, `.ovpn` is much harder and much slower.** \n\nHere is why you should **NOT** use `.ovpn`:\n\n1. **WireGuard cannot open it:** You cannot import `.ovpn` files into your WireGuard app. You would have to download and install a completely separate software (OpenVPN GUI).\n2. **Requires extra passwords:** OpenVPN forces you to copy and paste special OpenVPN usernames and passwords from the website.\n3. **Much slower:** OpenVPN uses heavy encryption overhead. WireGuard is **3x to 5x faster** than OpenVPN.\n\n---\n\n### WireGuard (`.conf`) is already 99% done:\n\nYou already have the **WireGuard app** open on your screen right now!\n\nJust:\n1. **Scroll back up** to the top of that webpage.\n2. Under **WireGuard configuration**, click the purple **\"Create\"** button next to **`US-FREE#109`**.\n3. It downloads the `.conf` file instantly.\n4. Drag or import that file into your WireGuard app and click **Activate**!","thinking":"OpenVPN config files.\n    *   **Setup Difficulty**: OpenVPN generally has a more complex setup compared to WireGuard.\n\n3.  **Answer the Question**:\n    *   **Summary**: `.ovpn` files are for OpenVPN (older, more complex) and are not usable in WireGuard. WireGuard, in general, is easier to set up.\n\nSummary:\n`.ovpn` configuration files are specific to OpenVPN, an older VPN protocol; they're not compatible with WireGuard. Setup for OpenVPN is typically more complex than for WireGuard.\n\n\n"}
